# Line endings, decided once.
#
# Prettier checks against LF, and CI runs on Linux, so a Windows contributor
# whose Git is configured with `core.autocrlf=true` gets a working tree full of
# CRLF and a format check that fails on every file — while the same commit
# passes in CI. Normalising here makes the checkout identical on every platform
# and takes the contributor's local Git configuration out of the equation.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so Git never touches the bytes.
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
